{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs26jVCkr6sEbCiDALnB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I dismissed finding R2F2 as not worth its cost. The verdict is committed as `d3553784` in `docs/reviews/wi-834/003-ADJUDICATE-f95988a.md`, with the `WI: WI-834` trailer and the commit hooks passing.\n\n**What the reviewer got right:** the WI spec's test list does say \"a review-next lane pauses with the obligation in the handoff\". No test builds a lane whose next step is a review, and none writes or reads a handoff.\n\n**Why it isn't worth adding:**\n- **The refusal doesn't look at the lane.** `session_service.launch_refusal` decides using only the clock, the call's role, and whether the work item's claim is active in the primary checkout. It never reads the lane's commits, review files or handoff. So a lane waiting for review and a lane waiting for rework take the same code path.\n- **That path is already tested.** One test refuses a REVIEW launch for an active claim. The new wrap-up test refuses BUILD and REVIEW inside the window on a lane with committed evidence, and admits BUILD after it.\n- **No kit code reads a handoff's next obligation.** `coordinator_guard` only takes a handoff's session prompt when a relaunch is requested, and relaunch requests are refused inside the window. The coordinator writes the handoff as prose. The one piece the code owns is the close-down instruction asking for it, and a test already checks that.\n- **The test asked for would only check itself.** It would reach no new code and would assert the contents of a handoff file that the test itself wrote.\n\nI ran the relevant tests and all 5 passed.\n\nThe leftover problem is the spec's wording, not the code. That test-list bullet should be reworded at the lane's spine checkpoint, which is outside this ruling. There's also one small gap, which I noted but didn't rule on: after the window, the test admits BUILD but never checks that REVIEW is admitted too. Both go through the same branch.\n\nI left the `.requested` marker file untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":58055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"3e8b9ea2-e242-4334-a009-4deef348f9a6","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:59:39.117Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs26jDKTo5BmJ1pFdGCz"}
